 "callout": "<b>Why this sits alongside the GA4 dashboard.</b> GA4 only fires for bookings made on our own website, so it never sees <b>OpenRice</b> — around a fifth of Hong Kong covers — only partly captures <b>Google Reserve</b>, and is blind to walk-ins and the reception desks, which together are close to half of all covers created. That is why the two numbers move differently: GA4 reads <b>▲32.0% YoY</b> on website bookings while total covers created across every channel are <b>+30.8% YoY</b>. Read this as the fuller demand and channel picture — OpenRice strength, heavy walk-in and reception volume at Dim Sum Library and Shiro — not as a contradiction of the GA4 story."
